  "body": "About the `HTMLIFrameElement`'s `sandbox` attribute:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4759106/158823629-02c180cd-3903-4d4f-84ed-d2c9aa44954e.png)\r\n\r\nI am wondering what it is marked as \"readonly\"?\r\n\r\nI would have used instead:\r\n```idl\r\nattribute boolean anonymous;\r\n```\r\nIf you agree with me, I will submit a PR. Otherwise, I would be interested understanding this.\r\n\r\nMy understanding: \"sandbox\" is defined as a mutable attribute on iframe and as a constant attribute on \"window\". Whenever a navigation starts, a snapshot of the frame's sandbox is taken. Then conveyed to the Window the navigation creates (if any).\r\n",
